From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-sm8550: let the PCIe 0 GDSCs power off in s2idle

Mainline keeps the SM8550 PCIe GDSCs in retention when they are disabled
(967e011013ed, PWRSTS_RET_ON), so gdsc_disable() returns without touching
the hardware and the controllers and PHYs stay powered through s2idle. A
powered controller still needs its NoC path, which is why the sleep set
needs a PCIe memory vote (0018/0019 here) or the wake hard resets, and that
vote keeps DDR out of self-refresh and CX up for the whole sleep.

pcie-qcom now turns the link off whenever D3cold is possible and retrains
it on resume, so the GDSCs can collapse; Qualcomm's downstream pci-msm also
disables the PCIe GDSCs in its clock deinit. Let the PCIe 0 pair power off.
PCIe 1 stays in retention: on the AYANEO Pockets it carries the USB
controller the gamepad sits behind, and that path was not tested here.

On its own this changes nothing while the suspend OPP floor of 0019 is in
the device tree: the floor still holds DDR. A board that drops the floor
(the Odin 2 Portal append) then reaches AOSS, CX and DDR collapse, and its
wakes do not reset.

The pcie_0 half of Armada 0566 (armada-os/armada 8dc0be9ad27c), the same
form as ROCKNIX/distribution PR 3636 (Jacob Cook; Retroid Pocket Nova,
AYN Thor).
---
diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8550.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8550.c
index 80a44ff..5889199 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8550.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8550.c
@@ -3003,7 +3003,7 @@ static struct gdsc pcie_0_gdsc = {
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "pcie_0_gdsc",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
 	.flags = VOTABLE | POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE,
 };
 
@@ -3014,7 +3014,7 @@ static struct gdsc pcie_0_phy_gdsc = {
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "pcie_0_phy_gdsc",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
 	.flags = VOTABLE | POLL_CFG_GDSCR | RETAIN_FF_ENABLE,
 };
 
